From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vkd3d-shader: Copy propagation of out-of-range and inner-array stores (6530)

Backport of upstream vkd3d a87b1efb ("vkd3d-shader/hlsl: Don't invalidate
OOB constant derefs.", Elizabeth Figura) and 09b9f8ff ("vkd3d-shader/hlsl:
Fix invalidation of the wrong components in copy-propagation.", Francisco
Casas), into the vkd3d bundled with Wine 10.0 (1.14).

A store with a constant index past an array's end is legal in dead code
before shader model 6, and an unrolled loop leaves such stores behind.
Copy propagation invalidated components past the variable and wrote past
its own trace array. The heap corruption crashed the compiler depending
on the heap layout. Firefox's WebRender gradient shader
(ps_quad_gradient) took down its GPU process, and with the GPU process
disabled, the browser itself. Stores into an inner array also dropped
the outer index and invalidated the wrong components, so a later read saw
the value from before the store.
---
diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/libs/vkd3d-shader/hlsl_codegen.c b/libs/vkd3d/libs/vkd3d-shader/hlsl_codegen.c
index d11ff48..40df2ee 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/libs/vkd3d-shader/hlsl_codegen.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/libs/vkd3d-shader/hlsl_codegen.c
@@ -1518,19 +1518,34 @@ static void copy_propagation_invalidate_variable_from_deref_recurse(struct hlsl_
     else
     {
         subtype_comp_count = hlsl_type_component_count(subtype);
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_HLSL_NO_OUTER_OFFSET
+        comp_start = 0;
+#endif
 
         if (path_node->type == HLSL_IR_CONSTANT)
         {
+            uint32_t index = hlsl_ir_constant(path_node)->value.u[0].u;
+
+            /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 6530), backported from upstream vkd3d a87b1efb and
+             * 09b9f8ff: don't invalidate anything if the index is constant but out of range
+             * (such indices are legal in dead code, which copy-prop has to see first: an unrolled
+             * loop's last iteration); and keep the offset of the outer levels. Invalidating past
+             * the variable wrote past its traces: Firefox's WebRender gradient shader crashed
+             * the compiler, and with it the GPU process. */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_HLSL_OOB_INVALIDATE
+            if (index >= hlsl_type_element_count(type))
+                return;
+#endif
+
             copy_propagation_invalidate_variable_from_deref_recurse(ctx, var_def, deref, subtype,
-                    depth + 1, hlsl_ir_constant(path_node)->value.u[0].u * subtype_comp_count,
-                    writemask, time);
+                    depth + 1, comp_start + index * subtype_comp_count, writemask, time);
         }
         else
         {
             for (i = 0; i < hlsl_type_element_count(type); ++i)
             {
                 copy_propagation_invalidate_variable_from_deref_recurse(ctx, var_def, deref, subtype,
-                        depth + 1, i * subtype_comp_count, writemask, time);
+                        depth + 1, comp_start + i * subtype_comp_count, writemask, time);
             }
         }
     }
